                title: "The Modern Iceberg",
                subtitle: "Money, fame, self, technology — same patterns, new names",
                emoji: "💰",
                sections: [
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Level 1 Modern: The Obvious Ones", body: "The ancient false gods demanded rituals, sacrifices, and allegiance in exchange for provision, pleasure, protection, and power. The modern ones do exactly the same thing — they just don't require an altar.\n\nMONEY (MAMMON)\nJesus: \"You cannot serve God and mammon\" (Matthew 6:24).\n\nMoney isn't evil. But money as ULTIMATE source of security, identity, and meaning? That's Baal in a suit. The promise is identical: worship me and I'll provide. The sacrifice is identical: your time, your relationships, your health, your integrity.\n\n\"Hustle culture\" is a prosperity ritual. The stock ticker is a modern oracle. Net worth as identity is Baal worship with better branding.\n\nFAME\nFame promises what Astarte promised — to be desired, admired, worshiped. Social media turned everyone into a potential celebrity and everyone into a potential worshiper. Likes are offerings. Followers are congregants. Cancellation is excommunication.\n\nThe sacrifice: authenticity. You become what the algorithm rewards, not what you actually are. You perform identity instead of living it.\n\nBEAUTY\nThe beauty industry is a $500+ billion global market. Ancient Asherah poles were symbols of fertility and physical perfection. Modern beauty standards are the same pole, digitally enhanced.\n\nThe sacrifice: self-acceptance. When your body is never enough, you've given your peace to a false god that will NEVER say \"sufficient.\"\n\nThe pattern: Every modern false god offers exactly what its ancient counterpart offered. The packaging changed. The transaction didn't."),
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Levels 2-5 Modern: The Deeper Ones", body: "LEVEL 2 MODERN: LIFESTYLE IDOLS\n\nSelf (Pride / Ego): The Renaissance said \"man is the measure of all things.\" Social media said \"I am the center of everything.\" Selfie culture is self-worship with a front-facing camera. The shadow module showed how ego creates the illusion of separation. Ego-worship is the foundational false god — because every other false god ultimately serves the ego's need to feel special, safe, or superior.\n\nComfort: Ancient hedonism has evolved into on-demand everything. The sacrifice: growth. You can't transform in a comfort zone. Every spiritual tradition says the same thing — the path goes THROUGH discomfort, not around it.\n\nPleasure: Astarte's ritual prostitution has become the $97 billion global porn industry. Same neural pathways. Same exploitation of desire. Same emptiness after.\n\nLEVEL 3 MODERN: INSTITUTIONAL IDOLS\n\nPolitics: When partisan loyalty overrides ethics, your party has become your god. Politicians as \"saviors\" is Chemosh worship — trusting a national power to protect you instead of doing the inner work.\n\nScientism: Science as tool = excellent. Science as ultimate authority that replaces all other ways of knowing = Bel/Marduk worship. \"Trust the science\" from someone who can't explain the methodology is authority inversion (ERSS Indicator 2).\n\nEducation: When degrees become sacred artifacts and universities become temples, knowledge has replaced wisdom. Nebo (Babylonian wisdom god) in academic regalia.\n\nLEVEL 4 MODERN: SYSTEMIC IDOLS\n\nTechnology: Screen addiction mirrors ancient ritual patterns — same times, same locations, same repetitive behaviors, same altered states. AI as oracle. Algorithm as fate. \"What does the feed say today?\" is divination.\n\nLuck/Fate/Karma misapplied: \"The universe will provide\" without personal responsibility is Gad and Meni worship (Isaiah 65:11) — trusting fortune over agency.\n\nLEVEL 5 MODERN: THE ABYSS\n\nAt the deepest level, all false gods — ancient and modern — serve one function: they redirect worship, attention, and energy away from the source and toward a counterfeit.\n\nDeuteronomy 32:17 — \"They sacrificed to demons, not to God.\"\n1 Corinthians 10:20 — \"The sacrifices of pagans are offered to demons.\"\n\nWhether you read \"demons\" literally (spiritual entities) or psychologically (unconscious patterns that possess your behavior), the functional result is the same: something else is running your operating system.\n\nThe entire SunFlow curriculum exists to help you identify what's running YOUR system — shadow material, cultural programming, inherited beliefs, false gods — and reclaim sovereignty over your own consciousness.\n\nEvery false god, ancient or modern, promises the same thing: \"Worship me and I'll give you what you need.\" The truth that every authentic tradition points to is: \"What you need is already within you. Stop looking for it in idols.\""),
                ],
                reflectionPrompt: "If I'm honest — what am I giving my MOST consistent attention, energy, and emotional investment to? Is it the source... or a substitute?"
